  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p>Small, palm-sized blasters see widespread use in weapon-restricted areas. Hold-out Blasters are commonly found in the possession of undercover agents, gamblers, <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Scoundrels\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Scoundrels\">Scoundrels</a>, or <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Nobles\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Nobles\">Nobles</a> seeking to protect themselves. They are sometimes carried as a backup weapon for more lethal characters. </p><p>Because of its compact design, a Hold-Out Blaster Pistol grants a +5 <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Equipment\" title=\"Equipment\">Equipment</a> bonus on <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Stealth\" title=\"Stealth\">Stealth</a> checks made to conceal the weapon. A Hold-Out Blaster requires an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Energy_Cell\" title=\"Energy Cell\">Energy Cell</a> to operate. After 6 shots, the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Energy_Cell\" title=\"Energy Cell\">Energy Cell</a> must be replaced. </p><p><b>Inaccurate:</b>&nbsp;This weapon cannot fire at targets at Long <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>. </p>",
